# This host checks out with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF. Anything a Linux
# container executes must stay LF: a CR on the shebang line makes the kernel look for
# "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and the container dies with exit 127. server/Dockerfile also strips CRs
# defensively, but keeping them out of the checkout is the actual fix.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch line endings or try to diff these.
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.png binary

# The executable bit does not survive a Windows checkout, and git records mode from the working
# tree — so `gradlew` and the container entrypoint were committed 100644 and CI died with exit
# 126 ("found, not executable") on the very first run. Fixed with `git update-index --chmod=+x`;
# these are recorded here so the next person knows the mode is deliberate and load-bearing:
#   android/gradlew            100755  (CI runs ./gradlew on ubuntu)
#   server/docker-entrypoint.sh 100755 (the Dockerfile also chmods it, belt and braces)
